============================================================
 SC LAB M3-L2: RULE ORDERING CHALLENGE
 Pod: {{ pod_name }} ({{ prefix }})
 Gateway: http://{{ gw_ip }}
============================================================

SCENARIO:
The {{ pod_name }}-GW firewall has all the RIGHT rules but in
the WRONG order. A "Block All" rule is at the top, preventing
all legitimate traffic from passing through.

YOUR TASK:
1. Log into pfSense at http://{{ gw_ip }}
2. Navigate to Firewall > Rules > LAN
3. OBSERVE: All allow rules are BELOW the block rule
4. REORDER rules so that:
   a. Specific allow rules come FIRST
   b. Default deny comes LAST
5. VERIFY after reordering:
   [ ] DNS works (nslookup acs-p01.local)
   [ ] Web browsing works
   [ ] RDP to DC01 works
   [ ] Ping works
   [ ] Unauthorized traffic is still blocked

WHY ORDER MATTERS:
  pfSense evaluates rules TOP to BOTTOM.
  The FIRST matching rule wins.
  If "Block All" is first, nothing else gets checked.

CORRECT ORDER SHOULD BE:
  1. Anti-lockout (Web UI access)
  2. Allow DNS to DC01
  3. Allow Web traffic (80, 443)
  4. Allow RDP to DC01
  5. Allow ICMP
  6. Default Deny (last)

